From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:42:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: count dependency stats on publication, and
 deferrals

dep_stats works, items, same_lane, repeat, reached and dropped were counted
while resolving a command's dependencies, before flight reservation. A
command deferred after that (EBUSY) was resolved and counted again on each
retry: Zink on Honeykrisp showed 13.2 works per frame for 6 commands
(Luanti on the mini). Tally them per attempt and count them once the
command has published.

The deferrals themselves are a cost: a deferred command waits for a
retirement. dep_stats appends deferred (EBUSY retries) and its reasons,
per reporting site, by the backpressure bit that deferred it: asids,
channel, scenes, events, queue, lane entries, Work storage, flights. One
attempt can report more than one reason, so CPU-held dependencies (a
compute waiting on another queue's stamp, a native render waiting for its
producers) are counted where they return EBUSY, as deferred_cpu_hold.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
